  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu Australia Policing and Justice Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Vanuatu Australia Policing and Justice Program (VAPJP) aims to support Vanuatu Police Force (VPF), justice and community service agencies to provide fair, equitable and quality services that meet the needs of the community. VAPJP takes a two-track approach of maintaining services in the short-term and improving capacity for the long-term. This approach is delivered across three interconnected End of Program Outcomes (EOPO) which are: (i) justice and police agencies improve quality and reach of services to Vanuatu communities, particularly in their handling of cases involving women, children, and youth; (ii) women, children and youth are increasingly accessing state policing, justice and community services; and (iii) policing and justice agencies maintain public security and the rule of law.</narrative>
  </description>
